{"name":"Tasman","hex":"#bac0b3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tasman","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Dutch.","A male given name transferred from the surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tasman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Masked booby","blocks":[{"text":"The masked booby, also called the masked gannet or the blue-faced booby, is a large seabird of the booby and gannet family, Sulidae. First described by the French naturalist René-Primevère Lesson in 1831, the masked booby is one of six species of booby in the genus Sula. It has a typical sulid body shape, with a long pointed yellowish bill, long neck, aerodynamic body, long slender wings and pointed tail. The adult is bright white with black wings, a black tail and a dark face mask; at 75–85 cm (30–33 in) long, it is the largest species of booby. The sexes have similar plumage. This species ranges across tropical oceans, except in the eastern Atlantic and eastern Pacific. In the latter, it is replaced by the Nazca booby, which was formerly regarded as a subspecies of masked booby."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Masked_booby_at_Baker_Island_%2848614360607%29.jpg/330px-Masked_booby_at_Baker_Island_%2848614360607%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masked_booby"},{"title":"Dianella tasmanica","blocks":[{"text":"Dianella tasmanica, commonly known as the Tasman flax-lily or Tasmanian flax-lily, is a herbaceous strappy perennial herb of the family Asphodelaceae, subfamily Hemerocallidoideae, found in southeastern Australia including Tasmania. Its leaves are up to 80 centimetres in length, and the flower stem is up to 1.5 m tall. Blue flowers in spring and summer are followed by violet berries. It adapts readily to cultivation and is commonly seen in Australian gardens. Unlike other Dianella species, its fruits are toxic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg/330px-Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dianella_tasmanica"},{"title":"Tasman (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Tasman is a rare family name in the diaspora of Dutch people. The distribution of people with the surname varies from about 6000 in Indonesia to small numbers in Australia and New Zealand, while by 2007 only seven people with the name lived in the Netherlands. The most notable bearer of this name was the Dutch explorer Abel Tasman."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasman_(name)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Masked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg/500px-Masked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Masked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg/1280px-Masked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Masked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg/500px-Masked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"S. d. dactylatra in flight, Grand Turk Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMasked_Booby%2C_Grand_Turk%2C_TC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Parque_Nacional_Marinho_dos_Abrolhos_-_Ronaldo_Eduardo_Dil%C3%A1scio_%281%29.jpg/500px-Parque_Nacional_Marinho_dos_Abrolhos_-_Ronaldo_Eduardo_Dil%C3%A1scio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Parque_Nacional_Marinho_dos_Abrolhos_-_Ronaldo_Eduardo_Dil%C3%A1scio_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Parque_Nacional_Marinho_dos_Abrolhos_-_Ronaldo_Eduardo_Dil%C3